Subject: [PATCH 15/22] =?UTF-8?q?Fix=20SessionPrompt.continue=20empty=20us?=
 =?UTF-8?q?er=20message=20=E2=86=92=20API=20rejection?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Patch 0020 spawned the wake-up turn with a synthetic-flagged user
message whose text was the empty string. The path through
MessageV2.toModelMessagesEffect filters user-message parts and then
drops messages whose part list is empty. An empty-text part collapses
to length 0 in the model API messages, leaving the previous assistant
turn as the trailing message — and Claude rejects that with "This
model does not support assistant message prefill. The conversation
must end with a user message." The wake-up never executed.

Replace the empty text with a single "." so the part survives every
downstream filter. The synthetic flag keeps doing the same UI work it
already did — it suppresses the per-step user-message wrap (so the
model doesn't see "<system-reminder>The user sent the following
message: </system-reminder>" wrapping nothing) and the chat-UI render.
The model now sees a one-character user turn; the system-reminder
injection from patch 0017 ("Background tasks ready: ses_xxx, use
read_task_result(...)") drives actual behavior. Models reliably
ignore lone-dot user messages.

If echoing or other model misbehavior surfaces, follow-up is to
extend MessageV2.toModelMessagesEffect to emit a placeholder when
a user message would otherwise be empty — broader change, deferred
until needed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 packages/opencode/src/session/prompt.ts | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/packages/opencode/src/session/prompt.ts b/packages/opencode/src/session/prompt.ts
index e10dbe1..281711c 100644
--- a/packages/opencode/src/session/prompt.ts
+++ b/packages/opencode/src/session/prompt.ts
@@ -1321,7 +1321,18 @@ NOTE: At any point in time through this workflow you should feel free to ask the
       )(function* (sessionID: SessionID) {
         return yield* prompt({
           sessionID,
-          parts: [{ type: "text", text: "", synthetic: true }],
+          // Hivemind: non-empty placeholder. Empty text gets dropped in
+          // MessageV2.toModelMessagesEffect (parts collapse to length 0
+          // for empty-text user messages), leaving the previous assistant
+          // message as the trailing message in the model API messages
+          // list — which Claude rejects as "assistant message prefill".
+          // A single dot is the smallest non-whitespace content that
+          // survives every downstream filter; the synthetic flag still
+          // suppresses the per-step user-message wrap and the chat-UI
+          // rendering, so the model just sees a one-character user turn
+          // and the system-reminder injection from patch 0017 drives
+          // actual behavior on this turn.
+          parts: [{ type: "text", text: ".", synthetic: true }],
         })
       })

